WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:11.100
Today we are going to see how this new AI&nbsp;
is able to take a piece of text from us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:16.140
anything we wish, be it a squirrel&nbsp;
dressed like the king of England,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:23.340
a car made out of sushi, or a humanoid&nbsp;
robot using a laptop, and, magically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:31.800
it creates not an image like previous techniques,&nbsp;
but get this, a full 3D model of it. Wow.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:40.620
This is absolutely amazing. An AI that can not&nbsp;
only create images, but create 3D assets? Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:47.220
indeed, the result is a full 3D model that&nbsp;
we can rotate around and even use in our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:54.240
virtual worlds. So, let’s give it a really hard&nbsp;
time and see together what it is capable of.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:01:00.000
For instance, OpenAI’s earlier&nbsp;
DALL-E text to image AI was capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.260
of looking at a bunch of images of koalas, and&nbsp;
separately, a bunch of images of motorcycles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:14.220
and it started to understand the concept of&nbsp;
both, and it was be able to combine the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:19.920
together into a completely new image.&nbsp;
That is, a koala, riding a motorcycle.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:28.260
So, let’s see if this new method is also capable&nbsp;
of creating new concepts by building on previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:36.840
knowledge. Well, let’s see…oh yes! Here is a&nbsp;
tiger wearing sunglasses and a leather jacket,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:44.280
and most importantly, riding a motorcycle. Tigers&nbsp;
and motorcycles are well understood concepts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:51.000
of course, the neural network had plenty of these&nbsp;
to look at in its training set, but combining the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:58.560
two concepts together, now that is a hint of&nbsp;
creativity. Creativity in a machine. Loving it.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:06.660
What I also loved about this work is that it makes&nbsp;
it so easy to iterate on our ideas. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:12.420
first, we can start experimenting with a&nbsp;
real squirrel, or, if we did not like it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:19.020
we can quickly ask for a wooden carving,&nbsp;
or even a metal sculpture of it. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:23.640
we can start dressing it up,&nbsp;
and make it do anything we want.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:31.320
And sometimes, the results are nearly good enough&nbsp;
to be used as-is even in an animation movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:38.820
or in virtual worlds, or even in the worse cases,&nbsp;
I think these could be used as a starting point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:45.900
for an artist to continue from. That would save&nbsp;
a ton of time and energy in a lot of projects!

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:52.320
And that is huge. Just consider all the&nbsp;
miraculous things artists are using the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:59.640
DALL-E 2 text to image AI and Stable Diffusion&nbsp;
for, illustrating novels, texture synthesis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:05.400
product design, weaving multiple images&nbsp;
together to create these crazy movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:13.560
you name it. And now, I wonder what unexpected&nbsp;
uses will arise from this being possible for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.000
3D models? Do you have some ideas?&nbsp;
Let me know in the comments below!

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:25.320
And just imagine what this will be capable of just&nbsp;
a couple more papers down the line. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:32.880
the original DALL-E AI was capable of this, and&nbsp;
then, just a year later, this became possible.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:40.140
So, how does this black magic work? Well, the&nbsp;
cool thing is that this is also a diffusion-based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:46.380
technique, which means that similarly to the text&nbsp;
to image AIs, it starts out from a piece of noise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:52.740
and refines this noise over time to&nbsp;
resemble our input text a little more.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:58.440
But this time, this diffusion process&nbsp;
is running in higher dimensions, thus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:06.660
the result is not a 2D image, but a full 3D&nbsp;
model. So, from now on, the limit in creating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:14.100
3D worlds is not our artistic skill, the limit&nbsp;
is only our imagination. What a time to be alive!

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.080
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

